oreign troops were still there at the  moment we're trying to get people across  the land borders to uzbekistan  tajikistan and pakistan  and once people get to those bordering  countries what happens then  well so far it's been quite difficult to  get them to these countries once they  get there they should be processed by  the german foreign ministry the german  embassies on the ground  and um receive a visa to go to germany  however it's been very very difficult  for these people to get to the country  we've managed to bring  some people across  but what these people really need at the  moment are a verbal note it's a  diplomatic document that tells the  neighboring countries of afghanistan  that germany will take these people to  germany  so should the german government then  essentially be doing more to get afghans  out of the country and also provide them  passage to germany  absolutely absolutely i mean they were  they're about 50 000 people that are on  the official evacuation list that  includes people in danger and their  family members the german government has  so far  uh evacuated about 10 of that number and  a lot of people find themselves in limbo  because i mean today we we got the news  that  germany would accept more than 2 000  people from the humanitarian list but so  far these are mere words they have no  actions been following up with these  words meaning that if um we from kabul  if we send our people to the pakistani  border right now they'd have no way of  entering because despite having issued  words the german embassy in islamabad  for example has not been issuing these  diplomatic notes these verbal notes for  people to actually cross the border and  be transported to germany to safety  and give us an idea i mean is it still  possible to evacuate people who want to  leave or is this a window of opportunity  closing  no it's absolutely still possible it's  it's  the german government would simply need  to issue  these diplomatic nodes these verbal  nodes and then people could cross into  neighboring countries gets a permit to  stay there for a certain amount of time  before moving onward to germany this is  just not happening quickly enough  despite the assurances that it will  happen for certain people  also there are talks about the airport  reopening the pakistani  airline it has been flying into kabul  airport so there are definitely options  to evacuate the people  today who's been working with the  initiative kabul airlift thank you so  much for joining us here on dw

